[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SearchableGeometries.Ball","page":"API","text":"Ball(center, radius; p=2, active_indices=true, indices)\n\nConstruct a ball with center center and radius radius.\n\nArguments\n\ncenter::Vector{<:Real}: Center of the ball.\nradius::Real: Radius of the ball.\np::Real: p-norm.\nactive_indices::Bool: Whether to use active indices.\nindices::Vector{Int}: Indices of the active dimensions.\n\nReturns\n\nBall: The constructed ball.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If radius is negative.\nArgumentError: If p is not a positive real number.\n\nExamples\n\nusing SearchableGeometries\n\nball = Ball([0, 0], 1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SearchableGeometries.Ball"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SearchableGeometries.SearchableGeometry","page":"API","text":"SearchableGeometry\n\nAbstract supertype for searchable geometric objects that canb be queried by the package's public API. Concreate subtypes currently include BoundingVolume and Ball.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SearchableGeometries.SearchableGeometry"},{"category":"section","location":"#SearchableGeometries.jl","page":"SearchableGeometries Documentation","text":"","title":"SearchableGeometries.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Main-objects","page":"SearchableGeometries Documentation","text":"SearchableGeometries.jl currently provides:","title":"Main objects"},{"category":"module","location":"#SearchableGeometries.SearchableGeometries","page":"SearchableGeometries Documentation","text":"SearchableGeometries\n\nTools for representing and querying simple geometric objects used in search, intersection, containment, and bounding-volume computations.\n\nThe package currently provides three main geometric objects:\n\nBoundary convention\n\nMany predicates accept include_boundary=true. When true, points on the boundary are treated as contained or intersecting. When false, strict interior containment/intersection is required.\n\nTolerance convention\n\nSeveral methods accept tol=DEFAULT_BV_POINT_TOL. The tolerance is used to handle floating-point roundoff, detect nearly inactive dimensions, and decide whether values are close enough to geometric boundaries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SearchableGeometries.SearchableGeometries"}]
